  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Refusals (Prime Directive: refuse by name instead of posting something silently wrong)**\n- **A canned cycle with no feed is refused by name.** If `FeedRate` is missing or not > 0, the post emits `canned cycle G73 has no feed rate - refused: ...` through the post's `msg()` / `refuse()` path and writes no G7x/G8x. This applies to every post that writes a cycle with its own F: `tormach`, `fanuc`, `haas`, `sinumerik`, `mazak`, `doosan-dnm`, `grblhal` and `fanuc-lathe`.\n- **heidenhain** keeps its fallback to the hole chain's own feed (`ChainFeedRate`), but no longer falls back to the program's last modal feed. With neither feed, its existing \"missing/invalid positive cutting feed\" refusal fires.\n- **tinyg, carvera and tormach-lathe** post drilling as plain chain moves with their own F, so they need no change.\n- **`tormach.cps`: a cut with the spindle stopped is refused by name.** This covers G1, G2/G3 and canned cycles: `feed move G1 in operation X with the spindle stopped - no spindle start (S.. M3) precedes it; ...`.\n  - `spindleOn` is true from the preamble's `S.. M3` to the next `M5`. Every section ends in M5, so a later section that states no speed is refused too.\n  - A touch-probe section (a stated 0 rpm, #574) is exempt.\n  - The other spindle mill posts get the same rule in follow-up **#1359** (P2, effort:high, area:post). Every one of their conformance goldens is a bare legacy stream with no spindle, so doing it here would move about 120 more goldens.\n- `assets/posts/AGENTS.md` states the new law.\n\n**Goldens**\n- The `.cl` goldens are generator outputs that `golden_cl.rs` pins, so they are not edited. Instead, the new `crates/app/tests/common/legacy_program.rs` builds the streams the tests post:\n  - `with_cycle_feeds`: each `; CYCLE` marker gets its own chain's cutting feed. This is what `post::dump` synthesizes for a generated cycle.\n  - `as_program`: also prepends the records a real operation's stream carries: SetupName, OperationName, OperationKind, ToolKind, ToolDiameter, `TOOL`, `SpindleSpeed`.\n  - The post crate's `fanuc_post.rs` and `arc_planes.rs` include the same file by path, so the shared `nc/*.nc` goldens come from one stream.\n- **The Tormach goldens are runnable programs.** `conformance.rs` now posts the Tormach mill goldens for the **770MX** (`tormach-770mx.mch`, inch) instead of the generic `3axis-vmc.mch`. They now open `(Tormach 770MX)` and carry:\n  - `(SETUP: Setup1)`, `(OPERATION: Drill1 - DRILL - G54)` and `(T4 6MM HSS DRILL - DRILL D0.2362)`;\n  - `G53 G0 Z0` / `G30` / `T4 M6` / `G43 H4` / `S1500 M3`;\n  - an F on the G73 (`G73 X0.7874 Y0.3937 Z-0.9449 R0 Q0.7087 F2.36`) and on the tap (`G84 ... F29.53`, a 1.5 mm pitch at 500 rpm).\n  - The tool diameters are the ones `golden_cl.rs` generated each path with.\n- **`index_4face_microarc4.nc` showed the bug itself.** Its hand-built stream stated the spindle once. The old golden then cut sections 2-4 after their predecessor's M5 with no restart. The test stream now states `SpindleSpeed` per section, as `post::dump` does, and the golden gains `S6000 M3` (and the belt note) in each section.\n\n### Goldens regenerated (WRITE_GOLDEN=1)\n- `nc/drill_peck.nc`, `nc/drill_plate.nc`, `nc/tap_plate.nc` (Fanuc): an F on each cycle block, nothing else.\n- `nc/haas/`, `nc/mazak/`, `nc/sinumerik/`, `nc/doosan-dnm/`: `drill_peck`, `drill_plate`, `tap_plate`. An F on each cycle block, nothing else.\n- `nc/grblhal/drill_peck.nc`, `nc/grblhal/drill_plate.nc`: an F on each cycle block (grblhal refuses the tap, so it has no tap golden).\n- `nc/tormach/`: all 13 legacy goldens (`contour_disc_hole`, `contour_plate_with_hole`, `contour_tangential_lead`, `drill_peck`, `drill_plate`, `face_square_40x40`, `face_square_40x40_stepped`, `pocket_waterline_plate_with_island`, `pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island`, `slot_fullwidth_centerline`, `slot_wide_channel_rows`, `tap_plate`, `trace_plate_with_hole`). These are now inch programs for the 770MX with the full preamble.\n- `nc/tormach/index_4face_microarc4.nc`: `S6000 M3` in sections 2-4 (above).\n- heidenhain, tinyg and carvera goldens did not move. No UI snapshot PNG was touched.\n\n### Tests updated to post real programs\n`tormach_post.rs`, `tormach_end_units.rs`, `tormach_machines.rs` (`tap_on`) and `tormach_fourth_axis.rs` (a `SpindleSpeed` per section) used bare legacy streams. They now use `as_program`. Their assertions are unchanged, except `an_inch_machine_posts_every_length_and_feed_in_inches`: it skips the 770MX's belt-range note line, because the metric reference machine states no belt ranges.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/post_cycle_feed_spindle.rs`)\nEach one fails when its fix is mutated away:\n- `a_canned_cycle_with_no_feed_is_refused_by_name`: every cycle post. It fails with the tormach check disabled, with the fanuc check disabled, and with any heidenhain fallback put back.\n- `the_lathe_drill_cycle_with_no_feed_is_refused_by_name`: fanuc-lathe. It fails with the check disabled.\n- `a_tormach_cut_before_any_spindle_start_is_refused_by_name`: a bare contour (G1) and a fed bare G73 are refused; the same paths as programs post clean. It fails with the spindle rule disabled.\n- `a_tormach_section_after_m5_with_no_spindle_speed_is_refused`: it fails with the rule disabled, and also when `spindleOn` is not cleared at M5.\n- `the_tormach_drill_golden_is_a_runnable_program`: the G73 has a positive F, and `T.. M6` then `S.. M3` come before it. It fails against the old golden.\n\n## How tested\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post` (all debug suites, not `--ignored`). Before the test updates, 6 targets failed, all expected bare-stream fallout. After the updates they all pass.\n- Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (post suites 28 s, app suites 799 s, 0 failed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The PathPilot Hub run of the new goldens. Copies of `drill_peck` and `contour_plate_with_hole` (inch, 770MX) are in the user's hub-tests folder for that run.\n- The spindle rule in the other mill dialects (#1359).\n- The release-lane `--ignored` suites and the UI suites (no UI code touched).\n\nChangelog: Posts refuse a canned cycle with no feed by name (Tormach, Fanuc, Haas, Siemens, Mazak, Doosan, grblHAL, Fanuc lathe; Heidenhain no longer falls back to the last modal feed), and the Tormach mill post refuses a cut with the spindle stopped; the Tormach goldens are runnable 770MX programs.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nFixes #1357\n\nOverlaps tormach.cps with open PRs #981 #1047 #1101 #1113 #1124 #1126 #564 (user OK'd)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
